id: hac-c0y8
title: Implement coalesced protocol and typed trigger observation
description: "Negotiate Home Assistant WebSocket coalescing, dispatch single and array frames safely, and expose a typed bounded subscribe-trigger command with validated JSON inputs and complete agent documentation."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[4]: agents,automation,implementation,websocket
created_at: "2026-07-25T00:18:21.933Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T01:03:41.341Z"
deadline: "2026-07-28T00:18:21.933Z"
assignee: codex-root
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Application calls begin at id 2 after successful coalescing negotiation and all pending results/events are dispatched from single or coalesced frames; Inline/file trigger JSON and optional variables are validated before connect, documented with examples, and captured with positive bounded numeric controls; Actual built hassio passes live read-only subscribe-trigger acceptance and every supported formatter/help/schema gate; Release verifier, 100/100/100/100 coverage, docstrings, file-size, duplication, lint, TypeScript, ShellCheck, audit, Trivy, PM integrity, package smoke, and dry-run release all pass"
definition_of_ready: hac-1sdd research step complete and plan approved
goal: best-agent-home-assistant-cli
objective: implement-bounded-coalesced-trigger-streaming
value: Deliver the executable product behavior from hac-r2z9.
impact: Agents can observe automation-level semantics without a broad unfiltered event stream.
outcome: Typed tested documented and live-proven WebSocket streaming behavior.
why_now: Official and live contracts are verified and the current transport is incompatible with coalesced arrays.
parent: hac-r2z9
reviewer: unbraind
risk: high
confidence: 98
sprint: 2026-07-websocket-streaming
release: 2026.7.25
